  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a binary string SSS of size NNN, and a parameter KKK.\n\nYou are wondering whether it is possible to rearrange the characters in SSS such that the following condition is satisfied:\n\n\nSi≠Si+KS_i \\ne S_{i + K}Si​=Si+K​ for all 1≤i≤N−K1 \\le i \\le N - K1≤i≤N−K\nPrint Yes\\text{Yes}Yes if it is possible to rearrange SSS in such a way, and No\\text{No}No otherwise.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains 222 space-separated integers - NNN and KKK.\nThe second line contains a binary string SSS.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line Yes\\text{Yes}Yes if it is possible to rearrange the binary string accordingly and No\\text{No}No otherwise.\n\n\nYou may output each character in either case, for example YES\\text{YES}YES, yes\\text{yes}yes and yES\\text{yES}yES will all be accepted as a positive response.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\le T \\le 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤K&lt;N≤1001 \\le K \\lt N \\le 1001≤K&lt;N≤100",
      "∣S∣=N|S| = N∣S∣=N",
      "Si∈{0,1}S_i \\in \\{0, 1\\}Si​∈{0,1}"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n4 1\n1010\n4 3\n1001\n4 1\n1111\n4 2\n1110",
        "output": "Yes\nYes\nNo\nNo",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: The given string is already valid as S1≠S2S_1 \\ne S_2S1​=S2​, S2≠S3S_2 \\ne S_3S2​=S3​ and S3≠S4S_3 \\ne S_4S3​=S4​.\nTest case 222: A valid rearrangement is 1010\\text{1010}1010. The only condition required was S1≠S4S_1 \\ne S_4S1​=S4​."
      }
    ]
  },
